            "alt": "Ante Kovačić in the engine room doorway",
            "label": "Master, MV Nyren",
            "title": "Ante Kovačić",
            "body": "Split-born, navy-trained. Swears the Adriatic has two hundred anchorages and has personally slept in ninety of them.",
            "linkLabel": "",
            "linkHref": ""
           },
           {
            "src": "https://qvzbothxlrzeklcvdhzp.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/coastwise/crew-chef.jpg",
            "icon": "",
            "alt": "Marta Reid in the galley",
            "label": "Head of galley",
            "title": "Marta Reid",
            "body": "Cooked in two starred kitchens and left both for a galley with a view. First down the gangway in every harbour.",
            "linkLabel": "",
            "linkHref": ""
           },
           {
            "src": "https://qvzbothxlrzeklcvdhzp.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/coastwise/crew-guide.jpg",
            "icon": "",
            "alt": "Tom Ellery with binoculars",
            "label": "Naturalist",
            "title": "Tom Ellery",
            "body": "Sails every northern departure. Can tell a minke from a swell at a mile, and will wake you for it if you asked.",
            "linkLabel": "",
            "linkHref": ""
           },
           {
            "src": "https://qvzbothxlrzeklcvdhzp.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/coastwise/crew-purser.jpg",
            "icon": "",
            "alt": "Fiona Bell at the shed door",
            "label": "The shed, Oban",
            "title": "Fiona Bell",
            "body": "Answers the phone, holds the plan, and has re-routed more holidays around more weather than anyone afloat.",
